From 8b928579267724a79a7de362c579132e81814f53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RDoom <171243930+aeon1911@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 13:40:47 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 20/51] Switch Vulkan: skip dcache cleans on uncached memory,
 overlap frames, stop per-frame phase.log writes

- VulkanBuffer/VulkanImage know whether their memory is HOST_CACHED. NVK on
  Horizon maps HOST_COHERENT memory uncached, so the per-submit clean of every
  persistent buffer, the Unmap clean and the light buffer cleans were pure
  overhead (5.7 -> 0.5 ms per frame in Ryujinx). Cached memory is still cleaned.
- Frame overlap (rd_vk_frameoverlap, default on): the end of a frame submits and
  presents without waiting; the fence wait moves to the next BeginFrame/Update,
  any other submit, and level load, so the GPU draws while the CPU runs tics.
- NX_Phase wrote phase.log (open/append/close on the SD card) five times per
  frame and grew without limit; it now records each phase once.
- perf.log: Vulkan submit/clean/acquire/present/wait timings; the stabilizer
  counts Vulkan waits as waits. Session report lists Vulkan memory types.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
